</blockquote>
<p>I have no idea why this is in quotes, and don't think it needs to be.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Rakmou-leusan's wrath is coming.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This strikes me as odd. Throughout the rest of the article, it's clear that Alison is only trying to support Rakmou, who would weaken and die without blood. It doesn't make sense for her to fear its wrath when her cult has it on cosmological life support. The rest of the piece unfolds with her acting out in desperation, but her fear then isn't from being smote by her god, its from the things it defends them from.</p>
